.TH GILGAMESH 1 "2026" "Livyatan Design Suite" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gilgamesh \- photo or prompt to a watertight, mm-scaled STL
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gilgamesh
[\fIFILE\fR]
.br
.B gilgamesh chain
\fIIMAGE-or-"words"\fR [\fIHEIGHT_MM\fR]
.br
.B gilgamesh remesh
\fIIN.stl OUT.stl\fR [\fIVOXEL_MM\fR] [\fICLOSE_MM\fR] [\fB\-\-mm\fR \fIHEIGHT\fR]
.br
.B gilgamesh render
\fIIN.stl OUT.png\fR [\fB\-\-size\fR \fIWxH\fR] [\fB\-\-yaw\fR \fID\fR] [\fB\-\-pitch\fR \fID\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Bare invocation opens the window. The chain turns a photo (or, with a
text-to-image backend, a prompt) into a printable solid via a local
trellis.cpp reconstruction server, then welds it watertight. remesh welds
any STL watertight on its own; render draws a quick shaded preview PNG.
.PP
Text mode is optional: it needs
.BR phantasos (1)
on PATH or
.B TXT2IMG_CMD
set. Image mode needs neither, only the trellis.cpp server.
.PP
.B gilgamesh chain
writes its output to
.B TRELLIS_OUT
(default: the current directory), unlike the window which writes to
.BR GILGAMESH_OUT .
.PP
.B gilgamesh remesh
takes voxel size and closing radius (mm) positionally;
.B \-\-mm
.I HEIGHT
scales the result so its tallest axis is HEIGHT mm.
.PP
.B gilgamesh render
draws IN.stl to OUT.png on a transparent background, CPU only, no window.
Its flags are --size WxH, --yaw D and --pitch D:
.TP
.BI \-\-size " WxH"
Output size in pixels, both > 0. Default 1024x1024.
.TP
.BI \-\-yaw " D"
Camera orbit around the model's vertical axis, degrees. Default 30.
.TP
.BI \-\-pitch " D"
Camera elevation, degrees; negative looks down at the model. Default \-12.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TRELLIS_URL
The trellis.cpp server (the reconstruction step; you run it). Default
http://127.0.0.1:8080; set it when the server is on another host or port.
.TP
.B TRELLIS_OUT
Output directory for the
.B chain
subcommand (default: current directory). The window ignores it.
.TP
.B GILGAMESH_OUT
Output directory for the window (default ~/GilgaMESH).
.TP
.B TXT2IMG_CMD
Command taking PROMPT OUT.png for the words path (default: phantasos).
.TP
.B GILGAMESH_SEED
Reconstruction seed sent to the server. Default: a hash of the input
image, so the same picture reproduces the same mesh. Set an integer to
pin or re-roll.
.TP
.B GILGAMESH_RES
Reconstruction resolution (512, 1024, 1536) passed to the server when its
build supports it. Unset: the server's own default.
.TP
.B GILGAMESH_VOXEL, GILGAMESH_CLOSE
Chain-path remesh voxel size / closing radius in mm, defaults 0.35 / 0.8
(the remesh subcommand takes these positionally instead).
.TP
.B GILGAMESH_MIN_WALL
Minimum thickness in mm given to healed thin sheets, default 0.8 (two
0.4mm perimeters), floored at 2.2 times the voxel. Chain and remesh.
.TP
.B GILGAMESH_DUMP_DROPPED
Debug: set to a directory and the remesh writes every discarded body
larger than 5% of the kept one there as STLs. Chain and remesh.
.TP
.B GILGAMESH_WALL_REPORT
Debug: set (any value) to print an experimental, uncalibrated thin-wall
estimate after the remesh. Chain and remesh.
.TP
.B GG_REAL_GLB
Tests only: input GLB for the ignored real_glb_through_native_remesh
test. No effect on the binary.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR phantasos (1),
.BR jove (1),
.BR livyatan (7).
